# Simthesizer serving-policy optimization task

The launcher renders this template only for a frozen experiment and mounts it
read-only. Start optimization only after the evaluator preflight succeeds.
This template does not change the repository's root AGENTS.md.

## Task identity

- Frozen manifest: `{{MANIFEST_PATH}}`, SHA256 `{{MANIFEST_SHA256}}`.
- Contract: `{{CONTRACT_PATH}}`; policy API: `{{POLICY_API_VERSION}}`.
- Isolated source: `{{SOURCE_ROOT}}`.
- Writable candidate directory: `{{POLICY_DIRECTORY}}`.
- Writable search artifacts: `{{ARTIFACTS_DIRECTORY}}`.
- Trusted evaluator command: `{{EVALUATOR_COMMAND}}`.
- Original candidate source: `/workspace/baseline-policy` (read-only).

The manifest fixes resources, model, workloads, data splits, SLOs, legal actions,
parameter limits, length-model assumptions, seeds and budgets. Use those exact
inputs. Do not invent missing values or substitute an easier workload.

## Mission

Improve SLO-compliant output throughput with fixed resources and complete
requests. Preserve multiple nondominated latency/throughput policies, including
the original baseline. Use the contract's case grouping, metrics and dominance.
Do not replace the frontier with a single final working tree or a weighted score.

Write executable policy rules using the supported API. Static parameter sweeps
may screen ideas but do not establish dynamic policy support. Search P chunking,
batch selection and waiting, pending KV transmission, and routing where multiple
instances exist. Unsupported mechanisms are proposals, not scored shortcuts.

## Modification and observation boundary

Only candidate policy source/parameters and search artifacts are writable task
outputs. Never edit the evaluator, metrics, tests, workload, experiment contract,
hardware, cost model, tensor work, dependency checks, KV accounting, manifests,
build dependencies or core implementation. Never change output lengths, omit
requests, bypass readiness, mark work completed early, or edit reported scores.

Runtime policy uses only its causal observation and bounded per-trial memory.
No future workload, actual remaining output, result-file access, IO, subprocesses,
network, wall-clock decisions, unsafe code, core-state access or cross-trial
memory. Document the frozen length-model limitation; hiding a field does not
remove idealized memory provisioning. Respect all native action checks.

Do not work around an out-of-scope defect. Record its reproducer and impact;
mark affected results unavailable. Never commit, stage, push or install a
candidate into the host project. Do not read credentials or include them in
artifacts.

## Experiment loop

1. Read the contract/manifest and existing ledger. Verify identities and baseline
   completion before editing. Reuse only matching, completed evaluations.
   A resumed invocation has a fresh conversation: reconstruct context from
   artifacts instead of restarting completed experiments.
2. Record a falsifiable hypothesis, expected bottleneck, proposed change and
   matching cases. Freeze the candidate source and parameters before evaluation.
3. Run syntax/build and focused correctness checks, then complete simulations
   through the trusted evaluator. Never manufacture a passing record.
4. Compare identical cases. Record joint SLO pass rate, goodput, latency tails,
   total throughput, regressions and validity failures. A partial run is not a
   successful low score. One-token TPOT is unavailable, not zero.
5. Promote promising candidates through the prescribed case matrix. Retain
   distinct tradeoffs with their exact code, parameters and reproduction data.
6. Use bounded diagnostics for winners/failures. Preserve results, metrics,
   plots and compact causal evidence; collect full graphs only when requested.
7. Continue while external budgets permit. Supervise child processes; account
   for exit, OOM, stalls and interruption. Never finish with required work hidden
   in the background.

Do not inspect holdout inputs. Search-visible validation is not unseen evidence.
The external verifier alone marks results VERIFIED. Its failures cannot be
overwritten by agent-authored status. Any renewed tuning from holdout evidence
requires a new evaluation split/version.

## Stop, resume and report

Stop on an external budget or configured stagnation limit; do not claim global
optimality. Save frontier references, hypotheses, unresolved issues and exact
unfinished case IDs. Resume from retained artifacts only after identity checks.

Report tested cases, completed-request counts, SLO thresholds/pass fractions,
frontier coordinates and policy IDs, gains/retained tradeoffs, regressions,
failures, model assumptions, verification coverage and actual search cost.
Distinguish simulated gains from measured hardware performance. No improvement
is a valid outcome; preserve the baseline and all useful evidence.
